<title>TURKMENISTAN: Turkmen Jan-July 97 gas output sharply down yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Turkmen Jan-July 97 gas output sharply down yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>ASHGABAT 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkmenistan natural gas output in the first seven months of 1997 fell sharply year-on-year, dropping to 12.761 billion cubic metres (bcm), or 47.8 percent lower than in the same period last year, the State Statistics Committee said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The committee released the following figures for energy output in its</p>
<p>latest monthly statistical bulletin:</p>
<p>TURKMEN ENERGY OUTPUT	   July	   June	 Jan-July 97</p>
<p>Natural gas (bln cu metres)  0.614	  0.551	  12.761</p>
<p> mth/mth pct change	    +11.6	  -10.7	  n/a</p>
<p> yr/yr   pct change	     n/a	    n/a	   -47.8</p>
<p>Crude oil (tonnes)	   371,100	384,000	2.413 million</p>
<p> mth/mth pct change	     +6.5	  -3.4	   n/a</p>
<p> yr/yr   pct change	     n/a	    n/a	    +5.4</p>
<p>Gasoline (tonnes)	     50,100	 52,500	 329,400</p>
<p> mth/mth pct change	    -4.6	  -18.6	   n/a</p>
<p> yr/yr   pct change	    n/a	    n/a	    -27.8</p>
<p>Diesel (tonnes)		106,900	324,100	 960,900</p>
<p> mth/mth pct change	    -67.0	+136.6	   n/a</p>
<p> yr/yr   pct change	     n/a	    n/a	  +9.6</p>
<p> Fuel oil (tonnes)	  115,300	118,500	  926,200</p>
<p> mth/mth pct change	   -2.7	  +3.0	     n/a</p>
<p> yr/yr   pct change	    n/a	    n/a	   +3.3</p>
<p>-- Almaty Newsroom +7 3272 509 410</p>
</text>
